{
  "$comment": "Note types on person records (decision 78). Three of Rock's own types are kept and updated in place (rockType true), and three are new. Every type gets View security, because most churches lock notes down and the measured source did on nearly every type. 'viewers' and 'editors' name security role groups by Guid; everyone else is denied. Each type's 'weights' give its share of generated notes, in percent, for each audience: 'guest' (Prospect, Participant, and Known adults), 'attender' (Connected, Engaged, and Leading adults), and 'child' (under 18). A type with no weight for an audience gets no generated notes for it. A confidential type's notes never mention other staff, and only its own authors reply to them, so nothing leaves the people allowed to view it. Replies to any note come from the type's other authors when it has them. Text pools live in content/notes/<key>.json. 'authors' lists who writes generated notes on the main campus, by Cast person Guid, with weights; every other campus's notes are written by its campus pastor (see campusPastor).",
  "$staffComment": "Staff who write the main campus's notes. Each campus's campus pastor is named in configuration/staff.json (decision 198). A package from before staff.json picks each other campus's campus pastor from its generated households: the oldest Leading adult, or the oldest Engaged adult when it has none.",
